{"id": "section-body-05046", "title": "Changing Antiretroviral Therapy", "chapterId": "chapter-six", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MANAGEMENT OF HIV AND AIDS", "Management of Adult and Adolescent Living with HIV with Antiretroviral Therapy", "Changing Antiretroviral Therapy"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-05046", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Changing Antiretroviral Therapy", "runs": [{"text": "Changing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Antiretroviral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Therapy"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05047", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "There are multiple reasons that may prompt the need to change antiretroviral therapy. These can be grouped into two major categories:", "runs": [{"text": "There are multiple reasons that may prompt the need to change antiretroviral therapy. These can be grouped into two major "}, {"text": "categories:"}]}, {"id": "body-05048", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "ARV specific adverse events (toxicity)", "runs": [{"text": "ARV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "specific"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "adverse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "events"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(toxicity)"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05049", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Treatment failure", "runs": [{"text": "Treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "failure"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05050", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "When changing treatment due to toxicity, Change or substitute only the ARV suspected to be causing the toxicity on the other hand If changing due to treatment failure, the following should be observed;", "runs": [{"text": "When"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "changing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "toxicity,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Change"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "substitute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "only"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ARV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "causing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "toxicity"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other hand If changing due to treatment failure, the following should be observed;"}]}, {"id": "body-05051", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "It is never recommended to switch to monotherapy", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "never"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommended"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "switch"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monotherapy"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05052", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Change at least two ARVs, preferably change all three ARVs (Do NOT retain the backbone)", "runs": [{"text": "Change"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "at"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "least"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "two"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ARVs,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "preferably"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "change"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "all"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "three"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ARVs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Do"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "NOT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "retain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "backbone)"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05053", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "When making ARV selection, opt for drugs that haven't been previously used and don't have cross-resistance, overlapping toxicities, or drug-drug interactions", "runs": [{"text": "When"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "making"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ARV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "selection,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "opt"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "drugs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "haven't"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "been"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "previously"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "used"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "don't"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "have"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cross-resistance, overlapping toxicities, or drug-drug interactions"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05054", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Lamivudine has the advantage of reducing HIV viral fitness and increasing susceptibility to AZT and therefore should be retained when changing the failing regimen", "runs": [{"text": "Lamivudine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "advantage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reducing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "HIV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "viral"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fitness"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increasing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "susceptibility"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AZT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "therefore"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should be retained when changing the failing regimen"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1741"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Management of hiv and aids", "start": "body-05046", "end": "body-05054"}}